retval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be inactive), or the\0A *         library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_aead_decrypt_setup(psa_aead_operation_t *operation,\0A                                    mbedtls_svc_key_id_t key,\0A                                    psa_algorithm_t alg);\0A\0A/** Generate a random nonce for an authenticated encryption operation.\0A *\0A * This function generates a random nonce for the authenticated encryption\0A * operation with an appropriate size for the chosen algorithm, key type\0A * and key size.\0A *\0A * The application must call psa_aead_encrypt_setup() before\0A * calling this function.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_aead_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     Active AEAD operation.\0A * \5Cparam[out] nonce            Buffer where the generated nonce is to be\0A *                              written.\0A * \5Cparam nonce_size            Size of the \5Cp nonce buffer in bytes.\0A * \5Cparam[out] nonce_length     On success, the number of bytes of the\0A *                              generated nonce.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL\0A *         The size of the \5Cp nonce buffer is too small.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be an active aead encrypt\0A *         operation, with no nonce set), or the library has not been\0A *         previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_aead_generate_nonce(psa_aead_operation_t *operation,\0A                                     uint8_t *nonce,\0A                                     size_t nonce_size,\0A                                     size_t *nonce_length);\0A\0A/** Set the nonce for an authenticated encryption or decryption operation.\0A *\0A * This function sets the nonce for the authenticated\0A * encryption or decryption operation.\0A *\0A * The application must call psa_aead_encrypt_setup() or\0A * psa_aead_decrypt_setup() before calling this function.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_aead_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cnote When encrypting, applications should use psa_aead_generate_nonce()\0A * instead of this function, unless implementing a protocol that requires\0A * a non-random IV.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     Active AEAD operation.\0A * \5Cparam[in] nonce             Buffer containing the nonce to use.\0A * \5Cparam nonce_length          Size of the nonce in bytes.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The size of \5Cp nonce is not acceptable for the chosen algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active, with no nonce\0A *         set), or the library has not been previously initialized\0A *         by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_aead_set_nonce(psa_aead_operation_t *operation,\0A                                const uint8_t *nonce,\0A                                size_t nonce_length);\0A\0A/** Declare the lengths of the message and additional data for AEAD.\0A *\0A * The application must call this function before calling\0A * psa_aead_update_ad() or psa_aead_update() if the algorithm for\0A * the operation requires it. If the algorithm does not require it,\0A * calling this function is optional, but if this function is called\0A * then the implementation must enforce the lengths.\0A *\0A * You may call this function before or after setting the nonce with\0A * psa_aead_set_nonce() or psa_aead_generate_nonce().\0A *\0A * - For #PSA_ALG_CCM, calling this function is required.\0A * - For the other AEAD algorithms defined in this specification, calling\0A *   this function is not required.\0A * - For vendor-defined algorithm, refer to the vendor documentation.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_aead_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation     Active AEAD operation.\0A * \5Cparam ad_length             Size of the non-encrypted additional\0A *                              authenticated data in bytes.\0A * \5Cparam plaintext_length      Size of the plaintext to encrypt in bytes.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         At least one of the lengths is not acceptable for the chosen\0A *         algorithm.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription